g\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/L\u00fc Liu-liang\">L\u00fc Liu-liang</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107367512\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107367512\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3646136</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 1 \u2014 L\u00fc Kung</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">Fang Chao-ying</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<p><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"550\" data-page-number=\"550\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/562\" data-page-index=\"562\" data-page-quality=\"3\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/562\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;562\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>L\u00dc</b> Kung \u5442\u5bae (<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14767791\">.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip{cursor:help;border-bottom:thin dotted cornflowerblue}.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip-nodash{border-bottom:none}</style><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u9577\u97f3, \u84bc\u5ff1,&#32;<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u91d1\u9580), Sept. 28, 1603\u20131664, May 13, official, was a native of Wu-chin, Kiangnan. He emerged from the examination of 1647 with the rank of <i>optimus</i> or <i>chuang-y\u00fcan</i>, being the second scholar to receive that distinction in the Ch'ing dynasty. The first was <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Fu_I-chien\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Fu I-chien\">Fu I-chien</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>] who obtained it in the preceding year. Appointed a first class compiler of the Hanlin Academy, he rose in 1653 to the rank of senior vice-president of the Board of Civil Office and early in the following year to be a Grand Secretary without having to adhere to the rule of seniority. After <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Ch%27%C3%AAn_Ming-hsia\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Ch&#39;\u00ean Ming-hsia\">Ch'\u00ean Ming-hsia</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>] was condemned to death in 1654 L\u00fc Kung was accused, among other offenses, of being Ch'\u00ean's confederate. He pleaded guilty, and asserting that he was weak and ill, asked to be retired. In the memorial which told&#32;<span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"551\" data-page-number=\"551\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/563\" data-page-index=\"563\" data-page-quality=\"3\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/563\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;563\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span>of his illness he used language that was considered in bad taste, stirring up still more criticism on the part of the censors. Nevertheless, Emperor Shih-tsu, hoping perhaps to cultivate the good will of his subjects in South China, retained him in office until 1655, or nearly a year longer. Even then L\u00fc was granted the additional title of Grand Guardian of the Heir Apparent before he was allowed to return home.\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-left\" style=\"color:inherit;width:40%;\" />\n<p>[1/244/5a; 2/5/40a; 3/3/30a; 4/4/23a.]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">Fang Chao-ying</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ch'\u00ean Ming-hsia"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Fu I-chien"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Lu W\u00ean-ch'ao"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/L\u00fc Liu-liang"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Fang Chao-ying"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period\n | volume   = 1\n | onlysection = lu kung\n | previous = Lu W\u00ean-ch'ao\n | next     = L\u00fc Liu-liang\n | from     = 562\n | to       = 563\n | notes    =\n | section_author = Fang Chao-ying\n}}{{DEFAULTSORT:L\u00fc Kung}}"}}}